Patch 7908 (ENHANCEMENT): players choose the player order: a device-to-player table in cellPad, started by a chord or the port, off until used.

Players choose the player order instead of the host slot: cellPad keeps a device-to-player table (libs/input/pad_join.h).

Not in force until a reorder is started, so the old rules (XInput slot order, INPUT_MODE, PAD_PAD_P2) stay exactly as they were.
Started by pad_join_request() (the port's Port Settings row) or by the chord Select + L3 + R3 held 2 s on any pad. Then every
device (XInput slot, the DualSense stand-in = slot 0, the keyboard) takes the lowest free player at its first button press, up
to four; a device that has not pressed is not given to the game; the joining press is swallowed until its device was released.
Join ends when every device that must join has, when four are taken, or on a new Start from player 1. After that a device that
disconnects frees its player, a later one takes the lowest free player, and player 1 is never left empty while another player
exists (the lowest other player moves up). The keyboard holds the end of join open only where INPUT_MODE makes it a player.
Rumble follows the player's device. g_pad_join_notify(joining, next_player) tells the port when to draw its on-screen text.

The chord and the keyboard rules read the wall clock only to time a held chord; the game never sees it.

Pure logic: installer/tools/pad_join_test.c (host test, no pad needed). Not tested with real pads.

